			<div class="content" id="post-content-4398819">
									

<p>So if I got this right then this is a grave and a tree on a field that make you have an existential crisis? I love it!</p>
<p>The only thing that pulled me away from the typical SCP feel (although this might have been intentional) is the way that Dr. Wallstone talks to D-53. It feels to me more like they have a deeper bond than just &quot;scientist&quot; and &quot;subject&quot; if Dr. Wallstone talks to him this way.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;examples</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;examples</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Dr. Wallstone:</strong> Hello? D-53? Robert, can you hear me?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>He calls him by his first name which indicates that they are closer to each other (I'm not even sure whether D-Class personell even have names.)</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Dr. Wallstone:</strong> It's part of the test. Just do it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Which for a scientist who is audio-logging all of this sounds a little unprofessional. It would be more convincing if he at least called it an &quot;experiment&quot;.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>There's only one little thing left which I'm not sure whether it is correct or not but:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Detained individuals are to undergo therapeutic treatment and amnesticized from ever encountering SCP-4622-1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If you remove the &quot;undergo therapeutic treatment and&quot;<br />
then you get:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Detained individuals are to amnesticized from ever encountering SCP-4622-1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Which is an incorrect sentence. As I said I'm not sure if this is allowed in english but I would definitely write it like this:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Detained individuals are to undergo therapeutic treatment and be amnesticized from ever encountering SCP-4622-1.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I hope this was useful.</p>

